<title>UK: UK card spending up yr/yr 21 pct in Jan - CCRG.</title>
<headline>UK card spending up yr/yr 21 pct in Jan - CCRG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Credit Card Research Group, representing major UK credit and debit card issuers, released the following consumer spending figures for January 1997 -</p>
<p> CARD EXPENDITURE (in mln stg) *   Jan 97    Jan 96   % change</p>
<p> All sectors - total		   6,942     5,737    21.0</p>
<p> Food and drink			  1,743     1,456    19.7</p>
<p> Mixed business			    560	 500    12.1</p>
<p> Clothing				    423	 362    17.0</p>
<p> Household				   690	 571    20.7</p>
<p> Motoring				    943	 779    21.2</p>
<p> Entertainment			     362	 303    19.7</p>
<p> Hotels					189	 166    14.2</p>
<p> Travel					732	 601    21.7</p>
<p> Services				    551	 410    34.4</p>
<p>NOTE * figures adjusted for variations in the number of processing days between months. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
